WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:02.560
For trivial health problems like pain,

00:00:02.660 --> 00:00:04.500
common cold and so on...

00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:08.160
it's not advisable to have medicines unnecessarily.

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:11.280
But many a time doctors encounter patients

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:14.800
requesting medicines for such trivial problems.

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:15.780
So once,

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:19.740
a smart doctor just gave some sugar pills as medicine to them.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:21.040
And surprisingly,

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:25.200
the patients reported feeling better after consuming the pills.

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:29.460
So what miraculous power did these sugar pills have?

00:00:29.540 --> 00:00:33.840
Let's find out !

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:38.200
This effect was because of a psychological phenomenon

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:40.440
called the Placebo Effect.

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:42.220
What does it mean?

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:44.880
Here the patients were given sugar pills,

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:48.440
but they thought that they were actually receiving real medicines.

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:50.760
So they had a positive mindset

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:52.660
that since they had taken medicine

00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:54.100
they would feel better.

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:57.840
And this led to a positive effect on their health.

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:00.760
This is the Placebo Effect.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:03.920
Now let's see another interesting example.

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:06.400
Some runners in a race were told

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:09.420
that they were given 'Super Oxygenated Water',

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:11.740
while it was just plain water.

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:17.080
But surprisingly these runners ran much faster than usual.

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:20.120
This led to the runners positive mindset

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:22.720
and they out did themselves.

00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:25.600
Pretty intriguing right!

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:29.360
In the first example that we saw, sugar pills did the trick

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:32.460
while in the second, it was the water.

00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:35.080
They are called Placebos.

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:39.260
So can you think of the applications of a Placebo Effect?

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:41.500
Give it a shot.

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:46.240
Placebo Effect plays an important role in the medicinal field.

00:01:46.460 --> 00:01:50.720
It's used to test the effectiveness of a new drug.

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:52.820
Let's say there's an organization

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:55.020
which has come up with a new pain killer

00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:57.740
and wants to check its effectiveness.

00:01:58.040 --> 00:02:00.520
Some of the volunteers in a research trial

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:04.980
are given a Placebo while the others the actual medicines.

00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:08.380
Now if the volunteers taking the actual drug

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:10.820
demonstrated a significant improvement

00:02:10.820 --> 00:02:12.740
over those taking the placebo,

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:15.360
then it means the drug is effective

00:02:15.460 --> 00:02:18.220
and we can use it as medicine.

00:02:18.460 --> 00:02:19.400
In this way,

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:23.240
it can be figured out if the new drug actually has any effect

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:26.720
or if it's just another Placebo.

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:29.760
We saw that a Placebo can be any substance

00:02:29.860 --> 00:02:32.300
that does not have any direct effect,

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:35.600
but it's used to change someone's mind set.

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:37.900
Now let's see one interesting example

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:42.620
where we don't even have to use a physical substance as a Placebo.

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:45.540
Normally a 30-minute exercise every day

00:02:45.740 --> 00:02:49.280
is enough for a human to lead a healthy life.

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:53.880
This is easy for people whose work involves physical activities,

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:55.720
like housekeeping.

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:58.360
But according to the study, it has been seen

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:03.420
that many housekeepers do not perceive their job as an exercise.

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:06.460
So, one interesting experiment was conducted

00:03:06.460 --> 00:03:08.740
with female house keepers.

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:11.300
The women were grouped in two.

00:03:11.660 --> 00:03:13.780
Group one was given a presentation

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:17.400
where it was told that the activities they indulge in at work,

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:20.000
are actually good exercises.

00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:23.660
And the other group wasn't given this piece of information.

00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:27.240
After a few weeks to see the result of the presentation,

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:30.900
these women were tested on a few parameters.

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:33.500
Surprisingly, the women from group one

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:35.660
showed quite a drop in body fat

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:38.300
blood pressure, and were healthier.

00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:40.280
But the ones from group two

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:43.740
didn't show any significant changes.

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:46.540
So what do you think happened here?

00:03:46.820 --> 00:03:48.920
This example takes us to a conclusion

00:03:48.920 --> 00:03:51.780
that Placebo need not be any physical substance,

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:54.960
it can be anything that our mind believes in!

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:58.240
Even if it's just a thought.

00:03:58.500 --> 00:03:59.360
Now here,

00:03:59.540 --> 00:04:01.300
just the thought that they were receiving a

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:04.500
good amount of exercise while they worked

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:07.180
changed their mindsets towards their job.

00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:11.600
And this resulted in a positive change in their health.

00:04:11.740 --> 00:04:13.480
Interesting, isn't it?

00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:17.440
We now know that having the right mindset matters.

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:21.560
Mindset effects our performances and abilities.

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:23.940
Now we all have a common notion

00:04:24.040 --> 00:04:26.880
that some of our abilities are innate.

00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:29.280
For example, many of us think

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:33.200
that people are either born intelligent or they are not.

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:37.180
We believe that the great scientists were born intelligent.

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:41.520
So is intelligence an innate ability?

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:44.180
Instead of having this fixed mindset,

00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:49.020
can we improve our intelligence by changing our mindset?

